    <div id="archetype-2-deepdive" class="concept-stream" style="margin-top: 2.5rem;">
      <div class="concept-step-card archetype-teal-border">
        <div class="step-card-header">
          <span class="step-tag badge-teal">2.2 ARCHITECTURAL DEEP-DIVE</span>
          <h3 class="step-card-title">Archetype 2: Industrial Deep In-Order Core (CVA6 / Ariane)</h3>
        </div>
        <p class="step-card-lead">
          Originally developed as <em>Ariane</em> at ETH Z&uuml;rich and now standardized by the OpenHW Group, <strong>CVA6</strong> is the premier industrial-grade in-order application core. By introducing a 6-stage decoupled scoreboard architecture and native AXI4-64b connectivity, CVA6 resolves the latency-serialization bottlenecks of rigid 5-stage designs while maintaining strict timing closure margins for commercial automotive and aerospace tapeouts.
        </p>

        <!-- 2.2.1 CVA6 Technical Breakdown -->
        <div class="sub-topic-card">
          <div class="sub-topic-head">
            <div class="sub-topic-title-group">
              <span class="pill-badge badge-teal">CORE 2</span>
              <h4 class="sub-topic-title">CVA6 (Ariane) &bull; 6-Stage Decoupled Scoreboard Core</h4>
            </div>
            <span class="sub-topic-spec-badge">~148 kGE &bull; SystemVerilog</span>
          </div>
          <p>
            CVA6 bridges the gap between ultra-lean research cores and commercial multi-issue engines by introducing scoreboard-driven concurrency:
          </p>
          <ul class="concept-list">
            <li><strong>6-Stage Decoupled Scoreboard Pipeline:</strong> Structured as PC Generation (PC Gen), Instruction Fetch (IF), Instruction Decode (ID), Issue / Scoreboard, Execute (EX), and Commit. The scoreboard tracks data dependencies, source operands, and busy flags for all in-flight instructions.</li>
            <li><strong>Out-of-Order Execution with In-Order Commit:</strong> When a long-latency multicycle instruction issues (e.g. integer divide, multi-cycle FP multiply-accumulate, or an unaligned memory load), subsequent independent integer ALU instructions are permitted to execute out-of-order. Instructions commit to the architectural register file strictly in program order, guaranteeing exact exception recovery.</li>
            <li><strong>Standard Industrial AXI4-64b System Bus Interface:</strong> Natively integrates standard ARM AMBA AXI4 master ports (AW, W, B, AR, R channels) with independent address and data phases. This allows CVA6 to interface directly with commercial DDR4/DDR5 controllers, PCIe root complexes, and standard FPGA IP blocks without protocol translation bridges.</li>
            <li><strong>Dynamic Two-Level Branch Prediction:</strong> Features a Branch History Table (BHT) with 2-bit saturating counters, a Branch Target Buffer (BTB), and a Return Address Stack (RAS). Mispredicted branch penalties are bounded strictly to 3 clock cycles.</li>
            <li><strong>16-Region Physical Memory Protection (PMP):</strong> Integrates 16 hardware PMP checker registers that validate every instruction fetch and data transaction against current privilege levels (M-mode, S-mode, U-mode), preventing kernel memory escalation attacks.</li>
          </ul>

